{"content":"🚨 **IMPORTANT: Pin `-f dryRun=false` with a guard test — this bug class regresses silently**

The fix itself is correct and verified end-to-end:

- `machine-sm.yml:23-26` declares `dryRun` as `type: boolean, default: true` — without the flag every rescue tick was a dry no-op (matches the live evidence in the PR description).
- `-f dryRun=false` is the right form for boolean inputs (same shape as the repo's own example in `factory-agents/docs/machine-factory-integration.md:206`).
- The callee forwards it correctly: `dryRun: ${{ github.event.inputs.dryRun || 'false' }}` (machine-sm.yml:69), and the `run-name` `(dry)` suffix only fires for `'true'`.

The concern: **nothing in the repo prevents this from being undone**. This bug already lived silently — the watchdog "believed it had saved liveness; it had filed a plan" — and only a live incident exposed it. The repo's established convention is to pin exactly this class of silent workflow bug with grep-guard tests:

- `test/machine_kit/factory_stub_ref_test.dart` — pins factory refs/secrets/trigger invariants of the machine stubs.
- `test/store_automation_guard_test.dart` (`daily-publish dispatch contract (#346)`): *"Cross-check every `-f key=value` a leg sends against the child workflow's declared inputs so the whole class of bug is pinned, not just this instance."*

The PR description itself says manual dispatches "must pass the flag explicitly too — worth remembering for any `gh workflow run machine-sm.yml` call". A guard test **is** the remembering mechanism; prose comments aren't.

Suggested test (follows the existing machine_kit style):

```dart
// test/machine_kit/sm_kicker_test.dart
import 'dart:io';
import 'package:test/test.dart';

void main() {
  // Live 2026-09-29: machine-sm.yml's workflow_dispatch input dryRun
  // defaults to TRUE — a flagless `gh workflow run machine-sm.yml` is a
  // dry no-op that only logs the plan, so the kicker's rescue tick saved
  // nothing (pr-1092). Pin the whole class: any dispatch site of
  // machine-sm.yml must state dryRun explicitly.
  final workflows = Directory('.github/workflows')
      .listSync()
      .whereType<File>()
      .where((f) => f.path.endsWith('.yml'));

  test('every machine-sm.yml dispatch passes an explicit -f dryRun= flag', () {
    final sites = <String>[];
    for (final f in workflows) {
      final lines = f.readAsLinesSync();
      for (var i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {
        final line = lines[i];
        if (!line.contains('gh workflow run machine-sm.yml')) continue;
        sites.add('${f.path}:${i + 1}');
        expect(
          RegExp(r'-f\s+dryRun=(true|false)\b').hasMatch(line),
          isTrue,
          reason:
              '${f.path}:${i + 1} dispatches machine-sm.yml without an '
              'explicit `-f dryRun=` — the input defaults to true and the '
              'tick becomes a dry no-op (live: pr-1092)',
        );
      }
    }
    expect(sites, contains('.github/workflows/sm-kicker.yml'),
        reason: 'the kicker rescue dispatch must stay under guard');
  });
}
